<title>INDIA: BSE figures of India carry forward trade - March 8.</title>
<headline>BSE figures of India carry forward trade - March 8.</headline>
<dateline>BOMBAY 1997-03-10</dateline>
<text>
<p>The following is the latest data, for the top 10 stocks by value, released by the Bombay Stock Exchange (BSE) for the carry forward or &quot;badla&quot; account ended March 8</p>
<p>.</p>
<p>SCRIP		  SETTLEMENT  AV BADLA  QTY    VALUE    % BADLA</p>
<p>			 RATE				 (RS MLN)</p>
<p>---------------------------------------------------------------</p>
<p>Reliance	     300	   2.37     698150 209.45    41.19</p>
<p>State Bank	   315	   2.50     656900 206.92    41.38</p>
<p>Tata Steel	   205	   1.66     724850 148.59    42.22</p>
<p>ITC		    440	   3.54     247700 108.99    41.95</p>
<p>MTNL		   280	   2.31     287700  80.56    43.02</p>
<p>BSES		   230	   1.92     259750  59.74    43.53</p>
<p>L&amp;T		    255	   2.16     203400  51.87    44.17</p>
<p>Tata Power	   141	   1.14     267500  37.72    42.16</p>
<p>ACC		   1765	  10.42	21210  37.44    30.78</p>
<p>Colgate		335	   2.80	94750  31.74    43.58</p>
<p>---------------------------------------------------------------</p>
<p>The average badla charges work out to 45.08 percent on an annualised basis against 22.12 percent in the previous carry forward account ended Feb 27.</p>
